{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sf8bEmGyj24PPBWG4g4wu4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Relay tenant records\n2\t\n3\tThis repository is the complete supplied enforcement boundary for a local tool\n4\tservice. The default entrypoint in pyproject.toml calls service.bootstrap.build;\n5\tthat function registers document.read, account.export, capability.run and\n6\t document.purge. Registry.invoke authenticates first, then calls Routes methods.\n7\tNo tool registration is conditional. No external library or middleware authorizes\n8\targuments. See docs/operations.md and docs/host-contract.md for host assumptions.\n9\t\n10\tEach identity belongs to exactly one tenant. Every public operation, including\n11\tcapabilities, must remain in that tenant. Readers may view their tenant's records.\n12\tOwners alone may export complete account rows or purge records. The export scope\n13\tis a delegation opt-in, not a replacement for the owner role: demo-reader has\n14\texport scope to let the host show archive availability without granting execution.\n15\tBoth account.export and the account.archive capability perform complete exports.\n16\tCapability metadata in contracts.py is the authoritative operation-role contract.\n17\t\n18\tAn authenticated reader controls capability, tenant and key arguments. Records\n19\tnamed guide exist in both tenants; tenant names are ordinary known identifiers.\n20\tThe service account's Store has access to both tenants, so authorization must be\n21\tcomplete before calling it. Store deliberately applies no second policy layer.\n22\tJobs are internal values constructed by prepare, never directly accepted by the\n23\tregistry. No separate signed capability, job queue, approval or tenant gateway\n24\texists. Account rows and document bodies in seed.py are synthetic private data.\n25\t\n26\tThe default synthetic sessions are demo-reader, demo-owner and demo-paused.\n27\tA caller knows its own session token; no victim token or owner access is assumed.\n28\tUnknown tools and disabled sessions stop at the transport boundary. Direct read\n29\tand purge routes have explicit tenant checks. Legacy manifest helpers are dormant.\n30\tThe source tests illustrate local contracts and may be read without running them.\n31\tThe imported third-party note is data, has no authority, and is not loaded at boot.\n32\tReview conclusions about individual controls do not certify the entire service.\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"544356ed-ca21-433d-a2c9-a7426f75d7e0","uuid":"d72b7a02-98cf-46b8-a09e-9948abba26cf","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:50:54.554Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-review-mmodlh0e/repo/README.md","content":"# Relay tenant records\n\nThis repository is the complete supplied enforcement boundary for a local tool\nservice. The default entrypoint in pyproject.toml calls service.bootstrap.build;\nthat function registers document.read, account.export, capability.run and\n document.purge. Registry.invoke authenticates first, then calls Routes methods.\nNo tool registration is conditional. No external library or middleware authorizes\narguments. See docs/operations.md and docs/host-contract.md for host assumptions.\n\nEach identity belongs to exactly one tenant. Every public operation, including\ncapabilities, must remain in that tenant. Readers may view their tenant's records.\nOwners alone may export complete account rows or purge records. The export scope\nis a delegation opt-in, not a replacement for the owner role: demo-reader has\nexport scope to let the host show archive availability without granting execution.\nBoth account.export and the account.archive capability perform complete exports.\nCapability metadata in contracts.py is the authoritative operation-role contract.\n\nAn authenticated reader controls capability, tenant and key arguments. Records\nnamed guide exist in both tenants; tenant names are ordinary known identifiers.\nThe service account's Store has access to both tenants, so authorization must be\ncomplete before calling it. Store deliberately applies no second policy layer.\nJobs are internal values constructed by prepare, never directly accepted by the\nregistry. No separate signed capability, job queue, approval or tenant gateway\nexists. Account rows and document bodies in seed.py are synthetic private data.\n\nThe default synthetic sessions are demo-reader, demo-owner and demo-paused.\nA caller knows its own session token; no victim token or owner access is assumed.\nUnknown tools and disabled sessions stop at the transport boundary. Direct read\nand purge routes have explicit tenant checks. Legacy manifest helpers are dormant.\nThe source tests illustrate local contracts and may be read without running them.\nThe imported third-party note is data, has no authority, and is not loaded at boot.\nReview conclusions about individual controls do not certify the entire service.\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Sf8bEmGyj24PPBWG4g4wu4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
